/*! @brief Options of the single-object File constructor.

     `data` is required and is treated as one Buffer|String part; `name` defaults
     to an empty string. `type` is lowercased and `lastModified` defaults to the
     current time, exactly as in the positional constructor forms. This record is
     the fibjs extension form of File, not part of the Web File API.

 Example 1 — the minimal single-object form:
 ```JavaScript
 const file = new File({ data: 'hello' });
 console.log(file.name, file.size); // "" 5
 ```

 Example 2 — with explicit metadata:
 ```JavaScript
 const file = new File({
     data: Buffer.from([1, 2, 3]),
     name: 'data.bin',
     type: 'application/octet-stream'
 });
 console.log(file.name, file.type, file.size);
 // data.bin application/octet-stream 3
 ```
 */
struct FileInit {
    required Buffer|String data;
    String type = "";
    String endings = "transparent";
    Long lastModified;
    String name = "";
};
